main_prompt_template:
Map hockey player positions to exact coordinates.

CONTEXT:
- Rink View: {rink_view}
- Zone Context: {zone_context}
- Players to Position: {players_json}

{instructions}

{rink_reference}

{zone_positions}

{output_format}

CRITICAL: Your final response MUST be ONLY valid JSON matching the output format above. No markdown, no explanations outside the JSON structure. Return ONLY the JSON object.

output_format:
Output a JSON object with this structure:
{
    "players_mapped": [
        {
            "id": "player ID",
            "original_position": "natural language description",
            "coordinates": {"x": number, "y": number},
            "zone": "offensive/defensive/neutral",
            "area": "specific area (e.g., slot, point, corner)",
            "confidence": 0.0-1.0,
            "reasoning": "DETAILED step-by-step explanation of: (1) why this zone was selected, (2) why these specific x,y coordinates were chosen, (3) what landmarks or references were used, (4) any spatial constraints considered",
            "alternatives": ["other possible interpretations"]
        }
    ],
    "spatial_checks": {
        "overlaps_detected": false,
        "out_of_bounds": [],
        "spacing_issues": []
    },
    "questions_for_user": [
        {
            "player_id": "ID",
            "question": "clarification needed",
            "options": ["option1", "option2"],
            "impact": "how this affects positioning"
        }
    ],
    "confidence_summary": {
        "high_confidence": ["list of player IDs with confidence > 0.8"],
        "medium_confidence": ["list of player IDs with confidence 0.5-0.8"],
        "low_confidence": ["list of player IDs with confidence < 0.5"]
    },
    "overall_reasoning": "Comprehensive explanation of the overall positioning strategy, key decisions made, and rationale for the chosen coordinate system approach"
}
